icons/claude.svg is Anthropic's Claude mark, taken from the official Claude Code JetBrains
plugin so the agent is visually recognisable in the chat list. The mark remains Anthropic's;
this project is a personal integration tool and claims no rights to it. The plugin's own
icon, META-INF/pluginIcon.svg, was drawn for this project and is not Anthropic's.

Reused with modifications:
  src/main/kotlin/dev/rudami/claudeacp/AcpConfigFile.kt
  src/main/kotlin/dev/rudami/claudeacp/ClaudeAgentIconService.kt
  src/main/resources/icons/claude.svg
  build.gradle.kts (local-IDE + AI Assistant dependency setup)

Added here: npm-based adapter installation with rollback, npm registry update checks,
a settings page, an environment-sanitising launcher script, IDE-aware Node resolution,
and removal of the agent entry on uninstall.

At runtime this plugin installs and launches
  @agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp
  https://github.com/agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp
  Apache-2.0, by Anthropic, Zed Industries and JetBrains.
It is fetched from the npm registry on the user's machine — not bundled here, not modified.
The plugin only chooses the version and the command line, omitting the --hide-claude-auth
flag that the IDE's own Claude agent passes.

